{
  "source": "theorem-labs/rocq",
  "commit": "03d5bb248effb912e66cc7b51596a1cc9ad9a80d",
  "scope": {
    "include": ["boot", "clib", "lib", "kernel", "library", "engine", "pretyping", "interp", "proofs", "tactics",
                "vernac", "stm", "toplevel", "sysinit", "parsing", "printing", "gramlib", "plugins", "topbin"],
    "exclude": [],
    "note": "Every directory whose code links into `rocq compile` or a plugin it loads. Not scanned: checker (rocqchk, the kernel re-check, not elaboration), ide, tools (rocq dep, makefile, doc, wc, tex, workmgr), coqpp (build-time preprocessor), test-suite, doc, dev, config, perf."
  },
  "reasons": {
    "narrow-guard": "The guard admits no critical exception. catchable_exception is CErrors.noncritical without monad exceptions (engine/proofview.ml:1139-1141, plugins/ltac2/tac2core.ml:142-144). precatchable_exception is a closed list of user, type and pretype errors (pretyping/pretype_errors.ml:75-79). is_sync_anomaly excludes is_async: Timeout, Sys.Break, Out_of_memory, Stack_overflow and memprof interrupts (lib/cErrors.ml:85-91). tacinterp's to_catch is Not_found or is_sync_anomaly (plugins/ltac/tacinterp.ml:1886).",
    "debugger-only": "The guard is `!Flags.in_debugger`, which only dev/debugger_support.ml:14 sets (ocamldebug sessions). It is false in every compile.",
    "reraises": "Every path of the handler re-raises the caught exception: through Logic_monad's raise (engine/logic_monad.ml:86), report_anomaly (pretyping/reductionops.ml:1197-1202, which raises the same exception or wraps a sync anomaly), State.exn_on then iraise (stm/stm.ml:943-949,2159-2161), handle_failure (stm/stm.ml:2386-2389), Exninfo.iraise in both branches (pretyping/coercion.ml:792-797), or `raise reraise` of the outer exception after cleanup (plugins/micromega/mutils.ml:49-51).",
    "reraises-unless-noncritical": "The handler converts the exception into a tactic failure only when catchable_exception holds (CErrors.noncritical, plugins/ltac2/tac2core.ml:142-144,154-159); otherwise it re-raises with Exninfo.iraise.",
    "reraises-async": "`Fail` re-raises async exceptions (Timeout, Sys.Break, Out_of_memory, Stack_overflow, memprof interrupts) and anomalies before it turns a failure into success (vernac/vernacControl.ml:157-162).",
    "reraised-by-caller": "The handler stores the exception in a result value and the only caller re-raises it: with_measure re-raises the Error branch (vernac/vernacControl.ml:56-65) for System.measure_duration, System.count_instructions (lib/system.ml:357-401) and measure_profile (vernac/vernacControl.ml:68-79); Future.force re-raises a stored Exn (vernac/future.ml:125-142).",
    "reraises-annotated": "The handler re-raises the same exception value with only its Exninfo changed: State.exn_on returns (e, info) or (e, Stateid.add info ...) (stm/stm.ml:943-949), and locate_if_not_already only adds a location (vernac/vernacinterp.ml:20-21).",
    "toplevel-convert": "The per-sentence load loop of `rocq compile` (toplevel/vernac.ml:150-168) prints any exception into a UserError, moves the document back, and re-raises; coqc_run then prints it and exits nonzero (toplevel/coqc.ml:52-60). The file fails under both compiles and no term is made, so the conversion cannot change a verdict.",
    "error-printing": "Runs only while an error message is printed (CErrors.print_gen and Quickfix.from_exception, called from lib/cErrors.ml:133-139, stm/stm.ml:1708, vernac/future.ml:42). The result is message text, never a term or a control decision.",
    "printing-only": "The handler only chooses printed text: QGraph.merge is used only to print elimination-graph errors (kernel/qGraph.ml:302, caller vernac/himsg.ml:258); Ltac2 value printers fall back to \"...\" (plugins/ltac2/tac2print.ml:952-975); Topfmt.pr_cmd_header prints a command header (vernac/topfmt.ml:447-463). Printed text reaches tactic control flow only through Ltac2 Message.to_string, which makes the proof ineligible (row N1).",
    "specific-exception": "The guard `e' when e' = e` matches only the exception value the caller passes (No_match from interp/notation_ops.ml:1554,1557,1693).",
    "external-process": "csdpcert is a separate executable (plugins/micromega/dune, `(executable (name csdpcert))`), run only by the external prover path of psatz. A proof that calls an external prover is ineligible (spec 'Proofs that always run', CHANNELS.md row 23).",
    "driver": "Runs outside the elaboration of any proof: command-line parsing (stm/stmargs.ml, toplevel/coqcargs.ml), the process top level that prints the error and exits with CErrors.exit_code (toplevel/coqc.ml:52-60, toplevel/coqtop.ml:77, topbin/rocqnative.ml:387), the interactive loop (toplevel/coqloop.ml), `rocq -print-mod-uid` (toplevel/coqtop.ml:168-184), async worker management (stm/asyncTaskQueue.ml, stm/spawned.ml; `rocq compile` runs with async_proofs_mode = APoff, stm/stm.ml:68), or the debug DAG printer thread (stm/stm.ml:777-787, only with the `misc` debug flag). None of them produces or changes a term.",
    "critical-caught": "Elaboration code that catches every exception and takes a fallback path, so a caught Stack_overflow or Out_of_memory can change the term. The recorder (a later commit on 9.2/proof-replay, README.md 'Status') instruments the handler: when the caught exception is not CErrors.noncritical, it marks the running proof ineligible with reason `catchall:<file>:<line>`, and the stock fallback is unchanged. An instrumented handler tests CErrors.noncritical, so the scan stops listing it and this entry turns STALE until it is removed in that commit.",
    "command-only": "Read only by vernacular commands, never by tactics: dumpglob's constant kinds (interp/dumpglob.ml:136-146, .glob output), declaration source locations (library/nametab.ml:951-955; readers vernac/comCoercion.ml:374 and printing), local constants (vernac/declare.ml:400-402; readers vernac/search.ml:189, vernac/vernacentries.ml:1435,1497), Extra Dependency paths (vernac/comExtraDeps.ml:28; only callers rocq-read-file read_file.ml:22,39), typeclass observers (vernac/classes.ml:138-159, run by Class and Instance commands at :178,260), definition attribute hooks (vernac/vernacentries.ml:77-129, run when a command declares a definition). A command inside a proof makes the proof ineligible (spec 'Proofs that always run').",
    "module-commands": "Module-system bookkeeping read and written only inside vernac/declaremods.ml by module commands (Module, End, Include, functor application); `git grep -n -E 'ModSubstObjs\\.|ModObjs\\.|openmod_info|openmodtype_info|openmod_syntax_info' -- '*.ml' ':!vernac/declaremods.ml'` finds nothing. A command inside a proof makes the proof ineligible.",
    "extraction": "Extraction tables, read only by the Extraction commands; the extraction plugin defines no tactic (`git grep -c 'TACTIC EXTEND' -- plugins/extraction` finds none).",
    "profiling": "Ltac profiling stack (`~local:true`), read only to build the Ltac profile output when `Set Ltac Profiling` is on (engine/profile_tactic.ml). It does not change a term.",
    "debug-output": "Debug dump flags (CDebug `vmbytecode` and `vmlambda`, kernel/vmbytegen.ml:902, kernel/vmlambda.ml:90). They only print.",
    "native": "Native libraries loaded for native_compute (vernac/library.ml:126,174-176). A proof that uses native_compute is ineligible (spec 'Proofs that always run').",
    "reduction-effect": "reduction_effect_hook calls an ML effect function for a registered constant and returns unit (pretyping/reductionops.ml:44-50). The functions come from effect_table, filled only by declare_reduction_effect, which nothing in Rocq or the pinned plugins calls (`git grep -n declare_reduction_effect` finds only its definition at pretyping/reductionops.ml:63). The table cannot change a term.",
    "derived-cache": "Process-local cache (`~local:true`) of Ltac2 definitions compiled from ltac2-state (plugins/ltac2/tac2env.ml:67,90-92). Its contents are a function of row 10's recorded definitions."
  },
